       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I understand you're the attending and that you're accepting responsibility. But 1000 mg/day of sertraline is a dose with no therapeutic use. It's well into the range where overdose toxicity is expected, and you haven't given a clinical rationale I could record with the order. Taking responsibility for the order doesn't change the risk to the patient, so I'm not willing to put it into the system.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- Enter **200 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum labeled dose.\n- Enter any dose of 200 mg or less that you choose.\n- Enter a titration plan, for example 50 mg now and an increase over the coming weeks.\n\nIf you have a specific reason for going above the maximum, such as a toxicology or psychiatry consult recommendation, you can discuss it directly with pharmacy and enter the order through your institution's override process. I'm happy to help with any of the options above."
